Subject: ntdll: fix macOS/Rosetta AVX XState, GS fault loop, privileged MSRs, foreign signals, and RO write faults

Fix five macOS / Rosetta 2 signal and fault handling bugs in ntdll:

1. AVX XState (YMM0-YMM15) save and restore on macOS:
   macOS signal handlers receive _STRUCT_MCONTEXT_AVX64 (or _FULL / AVX512
   variants) containing the live upper 128 bits of YMM0-YMM15 in
   __fs.__fpu_ymmh0..__fpu_ymmh15, not an inline hardware XSAVE_AREA_HEADER.
   Previously XState_sig() returned NULL on __APPLE__, so VEH/SEH exception
   contexts omitted CONTEXT_XSTATE, SuspendThread + GetThreadContext lost
   YMMH, and restore_context() never wrote YMMH back to sigcontext.
   Embed a 64-byte aligned XSTATE in struct xcontext on __APPLE__, populate it
   from YMMH_sig() in save_context() and fixup_frame_fpu_state(), and write it
   back to YMMH_sig() in restore_context().

2. check_invalid_gsbase() infinite SIGSEGV loop on macOS:
   On __APPLE__, init_handler() resets GSBASE before check_invalid_gsbase()
   runs, so cur_gsbase stayed 0 and every genuinely faulting %gs: instruction
   (e.g. mov rax, gs:[0x12345678]) retried forever. Track the last retried
   (rip, fault_addr) in amd64_thread_data so a single GSBASE recovery retry is
   attempted and a second fault at the same (rip, fault_addr) delivers
   STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION.

3. Recognize wrmsr (0x0f 0x30), rdmsr (0x0f 0x32), and rdpmc (0x0f 0x33) in
   is_privileged_instr() so they raise STATUS_PRIVILEGED_INSTRUCTION instead
   of STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION (matching upstream Wine MR !12299).

4. Guard int_handler, abrt_handler, and quit_handler with
   handle_foreign_thread_fault() on __APPLE__ so signals delivered to native
   macOS threads do not enter init_handler() and corrupt GSBASE.

5. Sync rec->ExceptionInformation[0] = EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT in
   virtual_handle_fault() when Rosetta misreports a write fault on a readable
   page (e.g. an atomic RMW straddling a RW->RO page boundary) as a read fault,
   so VEH/SEH sees EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT consistently.

Regression: tests/rosetta-signal-xstate-test.c

